<title>POLAND: Warta plans higher 1996 payout.</title>
<headline>Warta plans higher 1996 payout.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish TUiR Warta SA plans to raise the 1996 dividend from last year's 1.5 zlotys, the president of the company said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The management will propose a dividend ... we would like it to be higher than last year's,&quot; Andrzej Witkowski told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>He declined to give any details.</p>
<p>Witkowski said the higher payout would be possible thanks to a larger net profit in 1996, which is expected to amount to 17.4 million zlotys this year, 27 percent higher than last year. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
